    Figure 6.  Set Current Program File Screen after filename change\par
\par
\tab d) Explore Current Program Files.  The Current_Program_Files\par
        directory is open in a separate window.  Files can be\par
\tab    transferred in or out of this directory from other folders as\par
\tab    required using standard Windows Explorer techniques.\par
\par
  \tab    Note: this command is often used in conjunction with the\par
 \tab    \ul Explore Additional Program Files\ulnone  command as described in f)\par
 \tab    below.\par
\par
\tab e) List Current Program Files.  As shown in Figure 7 below, a\par
\tab    listing file of the Current_Program_Files directory is created\par
\tab    then opened in a separate window using the standard Windows\par
\tab    Notepad utility.  This file may be modified as necessary and\par
\tab    saved or printed if desired.\par
\par
\tab    Note: The \ul Set Current Program\ulnone  dialogue box as described above\par
\tab    in c) can be filled by applying copy and paste techniques to\par
\tab    this window to aid in minimizing manual entry where\par
\tab    applicable.  Existing filename characters can be used to\par
\tab    (partially) set the Current Program filename without having to\par
\tab    manually type the entire filename.  For example, the existing\par
\tab    file name \i PROGRAM.PAL\i0  can be copied and then modified into\par
\tab    \i PROGRAM1.PAL\i0  or \i PROGRAM2.PAL\i0 , etc.\page\par
